  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}({e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}({e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,{|}_{1}^{e}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|\\,{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =({e}^{e}-{e}^{1})-(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(e)-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1)) \\\\  & =({e}^{e}-e)-(1-0) \\\\  & ={e}^{e}-e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
